@startuml
title Current implemented direct-message write flow

actor Client
participant "Spring Security" as Security
participant "MessageController" as Controller
participant "MessageService" as Service
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "STOMP Broker" as Broker

Client -> Security : POST /api/conversations/direct/messages
Security -> Security : validate JWT + persisted session
Security -> Controller : authenticated user context
Controller -> Service : sendMessage(username, content, requestId)
Service -> DB : resolve recipient
Service -> DB : verify accepted friendship
Service -> DB : find/create normalized conversation
Service -> DB : allocate next sequence
Service -> DB : persist message with server timestamp
DB --> Service : persisted message
Service --> Controller : message DTO
Controller --> Client : 201 Created

note over Service,DB
Request UUID idempotency:
- same owner + same requestId -> existing message (200)
- foreign owner + same requestId -> 409 Conflict

Conversation creation and first-message persistence
are transactional. Database uniqueness resolves
conversation creation races.
end note

== Realtime delivery ==

Client -> Security : STOMP CONNECT /ws + access JWT
Security -> Client : STOMP CONNECTED + authenticated principal
Client -> Broker : SUBSCRIBE /topic/conversations/{conversationId}
Client -> Broker : SEND /app/chat.send
Broker -> Service : authenticated chat send
Service -> DB : authorize + persist message
DB --> Service : persisted message
Service -> Broker : server-authoritative MessageDto
Broker --> Client : MESSAGE /topic/conversations/{conversationId}

note over Service,Broker
Realtime V1 broadcasts only after successful message persistence.
HTTP and STOMP sends reuse the same message-service authorization,
sequencing, timestamp, persistence, and request-ID idempotency logic.
end note

note over Client,DB
Realtime V1 is implemented for the single-instance slice.
Reconnect/missed-event synchronization, read state, mutations,
replies, and offline synchronization remain deferred.
end note
@enduml
